0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T06:23:42-07:00","id":1210925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1210816#post1210816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Rich is out of town. This week's Monday Meeting Notes were done by Matt McElroy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are we sure Rich didn't just consume Matt's heartblood and take his form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T07:19:50-07:00","id":1210947,"title":"","content":"A year ago, I would be grousing about getting lunars before... well, any other type of Exalt. But the Devs have been doing such a good job of characterizing non-Solars and giving them a reason to matter in the setting that I'm actually excited to see where this goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T07:30:40-07:00","id":1210950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1210903#post1210903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the Lunar book will follow the same setup as the DB book, but with a chapter focusing heavily on the Caul and the Lunar dominions rather than the Great Houses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally am not betting on it. Lunars do not seem to be on the whole teamwork thing and pretty much all of the dominions shown so far have be single lunars working alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T07:57:40-07:00","id":1210957,"title":"","content":"Last Vance mentioned, Lunars is likely to cover Lunar dominions in some regard.<br /> <br /> I think what we're likely to get for the equivalent to the DB player options is a selection of Lunar mentors, the agendas they pursue and the resources they have available. Lunars being Lunars, and the Silver Pact being what it is, one of Creation's largest mutual aid networks, a young Lunar could opt to work with one mentor or move between multiple mentors, and choose to have their working relationships be as long or as short as required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T10:36:33-07:00","id":1211033,"title":"","content":"The Lunars book will undoubtably have more:<br /> <br /> * Supernatural Merits<br /> * Non-magical beast antagonist QC stats<br /> * Sorcerous initiations<br /> * Celestial Circle spells<br /> <br /> About as many:<br /> <br /> * Splat-exclusive Merits<br /> * Terrestrial Circle spells<br /> * Warstriders<br /> * Artifacts in general<br /> <br /> And less:<br /> <br /> * Martial Arts<br /> * Backer turnout, leading to less material in a following supplement like Heirs to the Shogunate, unless that following supplement is basically a bundle of more beasts, spells, and artifacts that non-Lunars can use. <br /> <br /> I say the last thing without any real bitterness, because I fully admit that the Dragon-Blooded and the locations they hold are more important to the game than the Lunars and their Threshold domains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T10:42:30-07:00","id":1211037,"title":"","content":"If we don't get it in the core Lunar book, I hope that the companion will have info about pre-Usurption Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:06:09-07:00","id":1211058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211037#post1211037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we don't get it in the core Lunar book, I hope that the companion will have info about pre-Usurption Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both previous books have talked about the First Age survivors/alumni.<br /> <br /> What has been missing is the Shogunate generation who were Chosen after the Usurpation, inheriting the legacies of the Lunars who died in the uprising and initial exile.<br /> <br /> This is Sha\u2019a Oka\u2019s generation, so he is the start of something new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:10:04-07:00","id":1211062,"title":"","content":"True, but I expect there will be some adaptation to Ex3 which needs to be done on the previous versions. Shogunate Lunars are really interesting as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:18:33-07:00","id":1211066,"title":"","content":"We\u2019re likely to see a lot more sorcerous workings used on territories, edifices, peoples, and tools passed down among mortals, as Lunar Exalted make use of Terrestrial and Celestial sorcery to bolster the power of their holdings, with none of the Realm\u2019s distrust of the art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:25:24-07:00","id":1211071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211033#post1211033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And less:<br /> <br /> * Martial Arts<br /> * Backer turnout, leading to less material in a following supplement like Heirs to the Shogunate, unless that following supplement is basically a bundle of more beasts, spells, and artifacts that non-Lunars can use.<br /> <br /> I say the last thing without any real bitterness, because I fully admit that the Dragon-Blooded and the locations they hold are more important to the game than the Lunars and their Threshold domains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Importance to the game doesn't necessarily correspond to importance to the fanbase; I note MoEP: Alchemicals outsells Abyssals, Sidereals and Infernals on DriveThru, despite going up later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:27:43-07:00","id":1211075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211071#post1211071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. Importance to the game doesn't necessarily correspond to importance to the fanbase; I note MoEP: Alchemicals outsells Abyssals, Sidereals and Infernals on DriveThru, despite going up later.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Lunar Kickstarter outperforms the Dragon-Blooded one, it will be because of the frustration their fans feel after two lackluster Editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:37:59-07:00","id":1211078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211075#post1211075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Lunar Kickstarter outperforms the Dragon-Blooded one, it will be because of the frustration their fans feel after two lackluster Editions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With maybe a dash of more people trusting OPP to run Exalted KS campaigns better. I'm not sure how many people sat out WHFW because of that, but I expect this one to go a lot better than the first, which may encourage people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:54:59-07:00","id":1211142,"title":"","content":"I think the Lunars will do a lot better than Dragon-Blooded. If it comes relatively swiftly (compared to DB), it will show that the game line is back on track. Also, I think a lot of people just like Lunars more. Everyone that I know (anecdotal, yes), is super-excited about the prospect of Lunars, while mainly needing the DB book for antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:21:25-07:00","id":1211154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211033#post1211033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I say the last thing without any real bitterness, because I fully admit that the Dragon-Blooded and the locations they hold are more important to the game than the Lunars and their Threshold domains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Elemental Super Soldiers in a deadly decadent court will always be a more popular concept than Furry I.S.I.S. <sub>Not that that isn't a fascinating topic for an RPG.</sub>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T15:28:58-07:00","id":1211183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211154#post1211154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, Elemental Super Soldiers in a deadly decadent court will always be a more popular concept than Furry I.S.I.S. <sub>Not that that isn't a fascinating topic for an RPG.</sub></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211066#post1211066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We\u2019re likely to see a lot more sorcerous workings used on territories, edifices, peoples, and tools passed down among mortals, as Lunar Exalted make use of Terrestrial and Celestial sorcery to bolster the power of their holdings, with none of the Realm\u2019s distrust of the art.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that \u201cdemigods who reshape the lands and peoples of the Threshold to better suit their whims and protect their own\u201d is a bit more interesting and nuanced than \u201cFurry ISIS\u201d, personally.<br /> <br /> Fantasy fairy tale lands and races without ever needing to go to the Wyld!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m hoping for kingdoms and societies that make Halta look like the boring and lazy effort that it was.<br /> <br /> Think Volibear and Ornn, of League of Legends\u2019 current lore. Also, the immortals of Shurima; Nasus, Renketon, and the pharaoh guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T16:21:33-07:00","id":1211206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211183#post1211183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think that \u201cdemigods who reshape the lands and peoples of the Threshold to better suit their whims and protect their own\u201d is a bit more interesting and nuanced than \u201cFurry ISIS\u201d, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but it's not as punchy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T17:25:39-07:00","id":1211232,"title":"","content":"Oh, nice to see some CofD stuff, specially some non-Dark Eras new content.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211058#post1211058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both previous books have talked about the First Age survivors/alumni.<br /> <br /> What has been missing is the Shogunate generation who were Chosen after the Usurpation, inheriting the legacies of the Lunars who died in the uprising and initial exile.<br /> <br /> This is Sha\u2019a Oka\u2019s generation, so he is the start of something new.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Uka the Boar and Rain Deathflyer (from Halta) would count are part of that generation too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-24-2018, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T17:27:28-07:00","id":1211233,"title":"","content":"Aeon/Aberrant/Adventure (&amp; Scion) materials are also very relevant to my interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-24-2018, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T18:32:46-07:00","id":1211254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211206#post1211206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but it's not as punchy.</div> </div> </div> </div>NB: The developers have said that comparisons to Daesh are off-base. Let the meme die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T19:20:25-07:00","id":1211265,"title":"","content":"Well if nothing else this gives me hope that Lunars aren't going to end up strangled under concerns requiring them to need to be inferior to Solars mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T20:11:03-07:00","id":1211277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211078#post1211078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> With maybe a dash of more people trusting OPP to run Exalted KS campaigns better. I'm not sure how many people sat out WHFW because of that, but I expect this one to go a lot better than the first, which may encourage people.</div> </div> </div> </div> If the Dragon Blooded Kickstarter delivers on time or early on not only the book but timely delivers the companion book and all of the extra's I think the future kickstarters for Exalted will all do much better. I think there is a lot of distrust from the core KS that they have a chance to dispel by getting this one right. I was not part of the core KS but this one so far to me seems to be run very orderly with the expectations stated upfront and a timeline which although seems a bit excessively long for deliverables, is still clearly stated and should be achievable by or before the estimated delivery date. Having all the text done for example means the time for release is much closer than the EX3 book was when the kickstarter was ran. I have the expectation they will deliver this one well and it will result in the Lunar kickstarter doing really well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T04:58:17-07:00","id":1211367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>drakor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211277#post1211277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Dragon Blooded Kickstarter delivers on time or early on not only the book but timely delivers the companion book and all of the extra's I think the future kickstarters for Exalted will all do much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rich has stated before that the estimated delivery date is only for the book actually being kickstarted. OPP doesn't hold the stretch goals to the same timeline. So, people shouldn't expect them to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T07:25:59-07:00","id":1211401,"title":"","content":"I've always been super excited about Lunars, even if I didn't like all of what other editions did to them culturally or mechanically. I look forward to seeing how they turn out in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4862-sequal","name":"Sequal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4862_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T13:03:19-07:00","id":1211519,"title":"","content":"Dixie Cochran reports in the Monday Meeting comments (with permission from Eric) that the title is &quot;Lunars: Fangs at the Gate&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T19:56:35-07:00","id":1211660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211519#post1211519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dixie Cochran reports in the Monday Meeting comments (with permission from Eric) that the title is &quot;Lunars: Fangs at the Gate&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This pleases me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T20:15:08-07:00","id":1211672,"title":"","content":"The fact that Rain Deathflyer comes of as the young junior partner backing Halta emphasizes the problem of First Age survivors being the default for Elder Lunars.<br /> <br /> Ideally the norm for Elder Lunars should be centuries old but Exalted post-contagion. Meeting a Shogunate survivor should be a big deal - and First Age survivors should be whispered legends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T20:41:04-07:00","id":1211676,"title":"","content":"Well, the Black Lion is apparently from a thousand years ago and was around for the contagion so that is at least one prominent shogunate era elder so far. Who knows how many more we will get in a book actually focused on Lunars or maybe mentioned in the realm book like him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T02:50:04-07:00","id":1211724,"title":"","content":"I don't like the name Fangs at the Gate. Feels a bit underwhelming. It's just a name, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T18:36:17-07:00","id":1213624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211367#post1211367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rich has stated before that the estimated delivery date is only for the book actually being kickstarted. OPP doesn't hold the stretch goals to the same timeline. So, people shouldn't expect them to.</div> </div> </div> </div> Good to know. If that is the case I hope they will eventually be able to give an estimated delivery date for the stretch goals materials. I saw in ask the devs that the outline for the information going into the Heirs of the Shogunate supplemental book is being worked on. I do hope the time frame for the KS ultimately proves to be the time frame for everything but I will definitely keep my expectations realistic on the time frame. Thanks Florin for the heads up on that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T04:17:06-07:00","id":1213732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>drakor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1213624#post1213624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good to know. If that is the case I hope they will eventually be able to give an estimated delivery date for the stretch goals materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, OPP has to set the estimated dates before a single stretch goal is reached. It would be pretty tough for them to come up with anything resembling an accurate estimate before the KS even started.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}